const approachBody = '<h1>From measurement question to a trusted system.</h1>' +
  '<p>We start with the business problem, make the smallest defensible change, prove that it works and leave your team with the documentation to own it.</p>' +
  '<h2>1. Diagnose</h2><p>Reproduce the issue, review the setup and agree which business decisions and metrics matter. <strong>You get:</strong> scope, evidence log and priorities. <strong>We need:</strong> an example of the issue, affected journey and read-only access. <strong>Typical duration:</strong> 1–3 days.</p>' +
  '<h2>2. Design</h2><p>Define the event plan, data-layer requirements, naming rules and destination mapping. <strong>You get:</strong> a tracking plan and implementation specification. <strong>We need:</strong> agreed event definitions, required properties and source-of-truth systems.</p>' +
  '<h2>3. Implement</h2><p>Configure GA4, GTM, server-side tagging, consent behavior, ad destinations or CRM connections in your accounts. <strong>You get:</strong> the agreed changes and a record of what changed. <strong>We need:</strong> minimum approved edit access and developer support where site code must change.</p>' +
  '<h2>4. Validate</h2><p>Test journeys across devices, consent states and domains, then compare outcomes with backend or CRM records. <strong>You get:</strong> a QA evidence log. <strong>We need:</strong> test transactions or records and confirmation of expected outcomes.</p>' +
  '<h2>5. Hand over</h2><p>Document configuration, ownership, decisions and maintenance steps. <strong>You get:</strong> implementation notes, ownership map and a recorded walkthrough where useful. <strong>We need:</strong> the people who will own the system after handover. <strong>Typical duration:</strong> 1–2 days.</p>' +
  '<h2>6. Monitor (optional)</h2><p>Review agreed events, destinations, alerts and data-quality changes. <strong>You get:</strong> a recurring health summary and action list. <strong>We need:</strong> monitored events, alert recipients and an escalation process.</p>' +
  '<h2>What should be ready?</h2><ul><li>Read-only GA4 and reporting access; GTM or platform access only where needed.</li><li>The key website or app journeys that should be measured.</li><li>Definitions for purchases, qualified leads and other important conversions.</li><li>Examples of what is missing, duplicated or not matching.</li><li>A business contact who can confirm definitions and coordinate technical changes.</li></ul>' +
  '<h2>Principles</h2><ul><li>Smallest defensible change.</li><li>Preserve what works.</li><li>Client-owned accounts.</li><li>Evidence over opinion.</li><li>Documented handover.</li></ul>' +
  '<p><strong>Read-only access is usually enough to start an audit.</strong> Edit access is requested only for changes you approve.</p><p><a href="/contact/">Describe your tracking problem</a></p>';
